.spec/decisions.md-35-## Decision rationale
--
.spec/decisions.md-46-ADR-023 and ADR-024 narrow *when* evidence is owed, not *whether*. Three rounds
.spec/decisions.md-47-of pinned-source analysis showed that the original full-fidelity M0 contract
.spec/decisions.md-48-required semantics no public SSH library exposes, so every candidate needed
.spec/decisions.md-49-open-ended fork surgery before any client could run. Splitting the contract into
.spec/decisions.md-50-a viability tier and an evidence-gated M3 tier restores a working macOS client
.spec/decisions.md:51:path without weakening host-key-before-auth, Keychain-only secrets, fail-closed
.spec/decisions.md-52-DNS, bounded memory, the public PacketFlow bridge, the rootless exec/stdio
.spec/decisions.md-53-relay, or the signed/notarized release requirements.

